<title>SOUTH AFRICA: MGX half year share rises, no div.</title>
<headline>MGX half year share rises, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Aug 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     15.9	  vs 12.2</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   4.22	  vs 3.04</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   6.49	  vs 4.67</p>
<p>    Tax			 2.27	  vs 1.63</p>
<p>    Interest income	 0.59	  vs 0.17 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		  24.01	 vs 22.17</p>
<p>Full name: MGX Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Although trading conditions for the remainder of the year were expected to toughen as a result of poor business sentiment and input costs to rise amid a weaker rand, the company was expected to achieve above average earnings growth for the full year, directors said.</p>
<p>It is company policy to declare a final dividend or capitalisation issue, they said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
